  "summary": {
    "plain": "Measurements of how 3 GeV electrons scatter from hydrogen and helium at very small angles. They pin down the strange-quark contribution to the proton's charge and magnetism far more tightly than before, and it is consistent with zero.",
    "technical": "A_PV(4He) = (+6.40 +- 0.23 stat +- 0.12 syst) x 10^-6 and A_PV(H) = (-1.58 +- 0.12 stat +- 0.04 syst) x 10^-6 for 3 GeV electrons at theta_lab about 6 degrees; G_E^s = 0.002 +- 0.014 +- 0.007 at <Q^2> = 0.077 GeV^2 and G_E^s + 0.09 G_M^s = 0.007 +- 0.011 +- 0.006 at <Q^2> = 0.109 GeV^2."
  },
